{"kind":"request","text":"DX-T1 (second recut): typed definition package on the second spike's\nsurface, with eight helpers. Replaces b104c368; amended by 4694a0ce\nafter 1761d819; its vocabulary is settled by the readability pass\n(05b20ffe) first.\n\nBuild the package that lets an author write a declared definition as\ntyped TypeScript which compiles to exactly the data the scope pins.\nChild of request 99c4756a. The library core is the second spike's\nlib.ts (branch spike/typed-definitions-20261028, commit f77e454a,\ndirectory spikes/typed-surface, 85 builders in six patterns: subjects\nwith the same verbs on each; one range form and one list form with a\nnamed typed element; conditions; one message shape for the sends;\nhandlers written like acts; modules as functions). The first spike's\nroom.ts is the client item of DX-T2.\n\nThe four-forms design rule of 1761d819 item 3 stands: builders compile\ninto the pinned bytes; derivations are computed, never authored;\nannotations are typed sidecars outside the pin; code is typed by the\ndefinition; platform data is referenced by type, never authored.\nOperands stay plain data with no methods; modules stay functions with\nexplicit dependencies. Downstream readers keep reading the pinned\nbytes.\n\nWanted:\n1. Package @generalbusiness/dap-define at packages/define from\n   spikes/typed-surface/lib.ts, with the surface the readability note\n   settles. Shallow types only.\n2. The eight helpers of 4694a0ce item 4, in that order: literals in\n   equals, differs and where; on.take for same-named slots; by and via\n   declared once with a typed sibling reference; grants and reasons\n   declared per definition, with compile emitting the per-act refusal\n   list; rules written beside their act and hoisted by compile;\n   quantifiers over an item; items and acts by value; errors reported\n   by act name and form with the offending form printed.\n3. Typed list elements without the spike's relaxed tsconfig flags:\n   every element typed from the act's record field, or declared with\n   elements(list, ...) for a list that is part of a fetched fact.\n4. Tests: both spikes' witnesses, pins unchanged. Exact pins for\n   lending, the live Counter (commitments.json, b5582434) and the grow\n   site; the grow room and the change lane equal in canonical spelling\n   until the canonical-spelling kernel item lands, then exact. The JSON\n   stays beside the source and a CI check fails when regeneration does\n   not reproduce a pin byte for byte.\n5. Documentation in docs/write-an-application.md: the typed form as a\n   way to write a definition, the six patterns, the four forms, the\n   data stays the unit of trust; the generated vocabulary page of the\n   readability note is linked, not copied. The attribute effect's\n   subject (4694a0ce item 7) is documented there. Plain English, lines\n   at most 79 characters, no comparisons.\n\nThe kernel is unchanged and no filing-gate item is opened by this\nhead. The spike directories are not landed; the package replaces them.","body":{"conditions":"After the DX-TR note lands. One gate, exact-head checker review, PD-2 note with the witness.","target_head":"06e4d33fe17937610891f29b5d1513b9e224edea","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}